Subject: client: keep asking the guest for the window size

Wires the resize module from the previous patch into the client, so the
guest's resolution follows the window after a display driver restart and
after Windows changes its resolution on its own.

- core.c: core_onWindowSizeChanged now only hands the size to the module,
  so no size is lost while the guest is away. core_resizeUpdate feeds the
  module from the main loop and sends the existing window-size control
  when it asks. An ask goes out only while the guest responds: the
  transport has the window-size feature, the guest read the previous ask
  (controlStatus), and no send failed in the last second. A failed send
  warns once until a send succeeds again.
- main.c: four hooks. core_resizeInit beside lgMessage_init,
  core_resizeSession at the start of each display session,
  core_resizeFrame where the frame thread accepts a new format, and
  core_resizeUpdate beside frameScheduler_update.
- CMakeLists.txt: builds resize.c; the tests add the resize-tests target,
  and every test target that builds core.c also builds resize.c.
- config_message_test.c: the existing cases follow the new rule (an ask
  waits for a frame, and a failed send is not counted), and new cases
  cover the glue.

No message is added and no message's format changes.

